; airline: a day of an airline, simulated from its record, then branched.
; What if a flight had left late, a hub had closed for a while, an
; aircraft had broken down? Each branch is the day again with one change,
; and those of the branches it's on, compared minute by minute with the
; runs it branched from. Once it's the same as one of them, after its
; change has stopped making a difference to what comes in, the rest of
; its day is that run's, so it stops there. What's kept of a branch is
; small: its change, where it rejoined, and what it came to. Kept for
; each, that's a history like git's, printed at the end, which the next
; round of what-ifs could start from.
;
;     node bin/slightc.ts -o airline examples/airline.slight
;     ./airline                     (reads examples/airline-day.sexp)
;     ./airline day.sexp
;     ./airline --time day.sexp     (and says how long each part took)
;     ./airline --record day.sexp   (prints only the base's record)
;     ./airline --json out.json day.sexp
;                                   (and writes every run's minutes and
;                                   flights, for charts)
;     ./airline --keep kept.sexp day.sexp
;                                   (and keeps every run in a file)
;     ./airline --from kept.sexp day.sexp
;                                   (runs only the branches not kept)
;     ./airline --every 60 day.sexp (checkpoints an hour apart; 0 for none)
;     ./airline --recover t/data/airline-recover.sexp day.sexp
;                                   (remedies for a disruption, checked and
;                                   ranked by services; see recovering)
;
; The day, in examples/airline-day.sexp: five aircraft, their twenty legs
; through a hub at ORD, the passengers changing planes there, the weather
; (legs that flew long, an airport closed for a while), the record of when
; each flight left and landed, and the what-ifs. The base is the day as it
; was, and the program checks that it flies every leg as the record says.
; (The record is made up, from the model; a real one would be what the
; model is calibrated against.) examples/airline-gen.slight makes a day
; the size of a small airline's, three hundred aircraft and about fifteen
; hundred legs; a made-up day has no record, so its record is what
; --record prints, appended to it.
;
; The model is in whole numbers (minutes from midnight, kilograms,
; passengers), so that two runs that are the same are the same exactly.
;
; - An aircraft is a process, and a minute is a tick. Each minute the
;   desk, the run's own process, tells every aircraft, and waits to hear
;   from all of them, so between minutes nothing is in flight, and the
;   whole day can be compared there.
; - At its minute, an aircraft in the air lands if it's due and the
;   airport is open, and otherwise holds; one going out of service is
;   withdrawn once it's on the ground, its legs cancelled; and one at the
;   gate leaves on its next leg once that's due, it's ready (40 minutes
;   after landing), any delay is over, and the airport is open. A leg
;   takes its block minutes, and any the wind added.
; - A leg is cancelled at its departure if a change cancels it, or if its
;   aircraft isn't where it leaves from (at the gate there, or bound
;   there) or is withdrawn: so cancelling a leg out cancels the leg back.
;   A swap gives two aircraft each other's legs ahead, at its minute.
; - Fuel: 300 kg a departure, and 40 for each minute in the air, holding
;   included. Passengers: the minutes each flight lands late, times its
;   passengers; connections missed, those whose first flight hadn't
;   landed 30 minutes before the second left; and seats on legs
;   cancelled.
; - What the day is at a minute, its digest, is all that decides the rest
;   of it: where each aircraft is, its next leg, and how long till it's
;   ready or due; and the passengers waiting to change planes, and how
;   long till they can. The totals aren't in it: what's been burnt, and
;   who was late, don't change what happens next. So a branch that's the
;   same as the base at a minute, with its change over, flies the rest of
;   the day as the base does, and its totals stay what they were apart.
;   A digest is kept as a hash (D209): a day's are 1,080 integers, however
;   big the airline. It's the same whatever order the desk hears the
;   aircraft in: each part (an aircraft's state, with its number, or a
;   connection's passengers waiting) is hashed, and the parts are added,
;   modulo a prime. Two minutes that differ add up alike only by chance,
;   as two values hash alike.
; - A change makes a difference to what comes in for a while: a delay
;   till the flight may leave, a closure while it lasts, quick turns while
;   they apply, and an aircraft out of service till the end of the day.
;   A cancellation and a swap make a difference only at their minute.
;   Before that a branch is its parent, minute for minute, which the
;   program checks; after it, the branch is compared with each run it's
;   on, oldest first.
; - The aircraft, legs and connections are numbered in the file's order,
;   and looked up by number, in tuples, so a minute's work grows with
;   what happens in it, not with the size of the airline.
;
; - Every half hour a run keeps a checkpoint, the state of the day then:
;   each aircraft's status and the legs it has left, and the passengers
;   waiting. A branch starts from the last checkpoint before its change
;   that holds for its parent, the parent's state and the branch's being
;   the same till then; then it runs only its own part, and the half hour
;   or less before it. The last line says how many minutes the branches
;   ran, and how many of them their own.
; - With --keep, every run is written to a file, its checkpoints too; with
;   --from, a later run starts from those, and runs only the branches not
;   kept, so a day can be explored a round at a time, each adding
;   branches to the day's file. The file holds a hash of what decides a
;   run but its changes (the model's constants and the day, without its
;   branches or its record), and is refused for a day it wasn't kept for.
;
; The expected output comes from t/models/airline.py.

(@include :fs)
(@include :http)
(@include "airline-services.slight")

; --- the model ----------------------------------------------------------------

(defun start () 360)                    ; 06:00, the day's first minute
(defun end () 1440)                     ; midnight, after its last
(defun turn-minutes () 40)              ; from landing to ready to leave
(defun change-minutes () 30)            ; from landing to boarding another flight
(defun fuel-off () 300)
(defun fuel-minute () 40)

; To be changed whenever the model's rules are, so that a history kept by
; an older model isn't used.
(defun model-version () 2)

(defun within? (t from to) (and (<= from t) (< t to)))

(defun open? (closed airport t)
    (nil? (find (lambda (c) (match c ((a from to) (and (eq? a airport) (within? t from to))))) closed)))

(defun turn (quick airport t)
    (match (find (lambda (q) (match q ((a from to _) (and (eq? a airport) (within? t from to))))) quick)
        (()        (turn-minutes))
        ((_ _ _ m) m)))

; --- the day's data -----------------------------------------------------------

(defun reading (records)
    (recv
        ((:open f)   (send f (list :read :sexp)) (reading records))
        ((:sexp f r) (reading (cons r records)))
        ((:eof f)    (reverse records))))

; The day: #(aircraft legs connects outs ins by-aircraft closed flew
; branches airports). The aircraft, legs and connections are tuples, numbered in
; the file's order: an aircraft is (tail base); a leg #(flight aircraft
; from to departure block passengers wind), its aircraft a number; a
; connection #(in out passengers), its legs numbers. outs and ins have,
; for each leg, the connections from it and to it, and by-aircraft each
; aircraft's legs, in order. The rest are the records of that kind, in
; the file's order, without their keyword.
(defun day-of (records)
    (let of (lambda (kind) (map cdr (filter (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) kind)) records))))
    (let aircraft (of :aircraft))
    (let tails (zip (map car aircraft) (range 0 (length aircraft))))
    (let flights (zip (map car (of :leg)) (range 0 (length (of :leg)))))
    (let wind (of :wind))
    (let legs (list->tuple (map (lambda (l)
                                    (match l
                                        ((flight tail from to dep block pax)
                                            (tuple flight (lookup tail tails) from to dep block pax (or-0 (lookup flight wind))))))
                                (of :leg))))
    (let connects (list->tuple (map (lambda (c) (match c ((in out n) (tuple (lookup in flights) (lookup out flights) n))))
                                    (of :connect))))
    (let numbers (lambda (t) (range 0 (tuple/len t))))
    (tuple (list->tuple aircraft) legs connects
           (index-by (tuple/len legs) (lambda (c) (connect/in (tuple/get connects c))) (numbers connects))
           (index-by (tuple/len legs) (lambda (c) (connect/out (tuple/get connects c))) (numbers connects))
           (index-by (length tails) (lambda (l) (leg/aircraft (tuple/get legs l))) (numbers legs))
           (of :closed) (of :flew) (of :branch) (of :airport)))

; xs by (key x), a number below n: a tuple of n lists, each in xs's order.
(defun index-by (n key xs)
    (fold/l (tuple/make n ()) (lambda (t x) (tuple/set t (key x) (cons x (tuple/get t (key x))))) (reverse xs)))

(defun day/aircraft (day) (tuple/get day 0))
(defun day/legs (day) (tuple/get day 1))
(defun day/connects (day) (tuple/get day 2))
(defun day/outs (day) (tuple/get day 3))
(defun day/ins (day) (tuple/get day 4))
(defun day/by-aircraft (day) (tuple/get day 5))
(defun day/closed (day) (tuple/get day 6))
(defun day/flew (day) (tuple/get day 7))
(defun day/branches (day) (tuple/get day 8))
(defun day/airports (day) (tuple/get day 9))

(defun leg/flight (l) (tuple/get l 0))
(defun leg/aircraft (l) (tuple/get l 1))
(defun leg/dep (l) (tuple/get l 4))
(defun leg/pax (l) (tuple/get l 6))

(defun connect/in (c) (tuple/get c 0))
(defun connect/out (c) (tuple/get c 1))
(defun connect/n (c) (tuple/get c 2))

; Changes name their flights, aircraft and airports, as people would.
(defun leg-named (day flight) (find (lambda (l) (eq? (leg/flight l) flight)) (tuple->list (day/legs day))))

; The changes of one kind, without their keyword: (:close "ORD" 690 840)
; is ("ORD" 690 840).
(defun changes-of (kind changes) (map cdr (filter (lambda (c) (eq? (car c) kind)) changes)))

(defun or-0 (v) (if (int? v) v 0))

; --- an aircraft --------------------------------------------------------------

; It knows #(number closed quick out desk cancels): which it is; when
; airports are closed and turns are quick; when it goes out of service,
; or #false; the desk to tell; and the legs changes cancel, by number. Its
; status is (:gate airport ready), (:air leg due) or (:withdrawn airport),
; and its legs are those still ahead, each #(leg from to earliest minutes
; departure): its number, the earliest it may leave (its departure, and
; any delay), how long it takes (its block, and any wind), and when it's
; meant to leave. Each minute it tells the desk its part of the digest,
; its events and the fuel it burnt; for a checkpoint, its state, its legs
; by number; and for a swap, its legs, then takes the other's.
(defun aircraft (ctx status legs)
    (recv
        ((:tick t)
            (match (fly ctx t (tuple status legs () 0))
                (#(status2 legs2 events fuel)
                    (send (tuple/get ctx 4) (list :done (part (list (tuple/get ctx 0) (state-of status2 legs2 t))) events fuel))
                    (aircraft ctx status2 legs2))))
        ((:state)
            (send (tuple/get ctx 4) (list :state (tuple/get ctx 0) (list (kept-status status) (map (lambda (l) (tuple/get l 0)) legs))))
            (aircraft ctx status legs))
        ((:legs)
            (send (tuple/get ctx 4) (list :legs (tuple/get ctx 0) legs))
            (aircraft ctx status legs))
        ((:take legs2)
            (aircraft ctx status legs2))))

(defun kept-status (status)
    (match status
        ((:air leg due) (list :air (tuple/get leg 0) due))
        (_              status)))

(defun aircraft-context (day changes i desk)
    (let out (lookup (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i)) (changes-of :out-of-service changes)))
    (tuple i (append (day/closed day) (changes-of :close changes)) (changes-of :quick-turn changes)
           (if (int? out) out #false) desk (map (lambda (c) (index-of-leg day (car c))) (changes-of :cancel changes))))

(defun legs-of (day changes i) (map (lambda (id) (leg-of day changes id)) (tuple/get (day/by-aircraft day) i)))

(defun leg-of (day changes id)
    (match (tuple/get (day/legs day) id)
        (#(flight _ from to dep block _ wind)
            (tuple id from to (+ dep (or-0 (lookup flight (changes-of :delay changes)))) (+ block wind) dep))))

; Its minute t: it lands or holds, it's withdrawn, legs it can't fly are
; cancelled, it leaves, as each applies; now is #(status legs events
; fuel), events being what the desk needs to know, (:arr leg), (:cancel
; leg) and (:dep leg aircraft), and fuel what it burnt.
(defun fly (ctx t now) (depart ctx t (scrub ctx t (withdraw ctx t (land ctx t now)))))

(defun land (ctx t now)
    (match now
        (#((:air leg due) legs events fuel)
            (match leg
                (#(id _ to _ _ _)
                    (if (and (>= t due) (open? (tuple/get ctx 1) to t))
                        (tuple (list :gate to (+ t (turn (tuple/get ctx 2) to t))) legs (cons (list :arr id) events) fuel)
                        (tuple (list :air leg due) legs events (+ fuel (fuel-minute)))))))
        (_ now)))

(defun withdraw (ctx t now)
    (match now
        (#((:gate airport _) legs events fuel)
            (let out (tuple/get ctx 3))
            (if (and (int? out) (>= t out))
                (tuple (list :withdrawn airport) () (append (map (lambda (l) (list :cancel (tuple/get l 0))) legs) events) fuel)
                now))
        (_ now)))

(defun depart (ctx t now)
    (match now
        (#((:gate _ ready) (leg & rest) events fuel)
            (match leg
                (#(id from _ earliest minutes _)
                    (if (and (>= t earliest) (>= t ready) (open? (tuple/get ctx 1) from t))
                        (tuple (list :air leg (+ t minutes)) rest (cons (list :dep id (tuple/get ctx 0)) events)
                               (+ fuel (+ (fuel-off) (fuel-minute))))
                        now))))
        (_ now)))

; Legs cancelled at their departure: one a change cancels, wherever it is
; among those ahead; then the next, while it leaves from somewhere the
; aircraft isn't, or the aircraft is withdrawn. So cancelling a leg out
; cancels the leg back too, the aircraft not being where it leaves from.
(defun scrub (ctx t now)
    (match now
        (#(status legs events fuel)
            (let due? (lambda (l) (and (<= (tuple/get l 5) t) (member? (tuple/get l 0) (tuple/get ctx 5)))))
            (out-of-place status (remove due? legs) (append (map (lambda (l) (list :cancel (tuple/get l 0))) (filter due? legs)) events)
                          fuel t))))

(defun out-of-place (status legs events fuel t)
    (match legs
        ((l & rest)
            (if (and (<= (tuple/get l 5) t) (not (at? status (tuple/get l 1))))
                (out-of-place status rest (cons (list :cancel (tuple/get l 0)) events) fuel t)
                (tuple status legs events fuel)))
        (_ (tuple status legs events fuel))))

; Whether the aircraft is where a leg from airport leaves: at its gate
; there, or bound there; a withdrawn one is nowhere.
(defun at? (status airport)
    (match status
        ((:gate a _)  (eq? a airport))
        ((:air leg _) (eq? (tuple/get leg 2) airport))
        (_            #false)))

; Its part of the day's digest at t: where it is, how long till it's ready
; or due, and its next leg, which says what it has ahead, the rest of the
; legs that leg was planned with (a swap moves them together, and a leg
; cancelled has gone by the time a change no longer makes a difference).
(defun state-of (status legs t)
    (let next (match legs (() ()) ((l & _) (tuple/get l 0))))
    (match status
        ((:gate airport ready) (list :gate airport next (max 0 (- ready t))))
        ((:air leg due)        (list :air (tuple/get leg 0) next (max 0 (- due t))))
        ((:withdrawn airport)  (list :withdrawn airport next))))

; --- the desk -----------------------------------------------------------------

; A run of the day: the desk is the run's own process, and the aircraft
; are its children. It knows #(day pids targets every swaps): the day;
; the aircraft, in the day's order; the runs to compare with, each (name
; digests from), oldest first; how many minutes apart to keep
; checkpoints, or 0 for none; and the swaps, each (aircraft aircraft
; minute). Each minute it tells the aircraft, hears
; from all of them, and keeps the books, #(ledger digests by-minute
; checkpoints). The ledger is #(totals waiting flown): the totals, (fuel
; late missed cancelled); the passengers waiting to change planes,
; (connection ready), once their first flight has landed; and for each
; leg, (off () aircraft) once it has left, (off on aircraft) once it has
; landed, or (:cancelled minute). Then the digests and totals by minute, and the
; checkpoints, each newest first. It gives (stop rejoined digests totals
; flown checkpoints): the minute it stopped, the run it rejoined there
; (or () at the end of the day), the digests and totals by minute from
; the day's start, as tuples, the legs, and the checkpoints, oldest first.
;
; It starts at the day's start, or from restore, a checkpoint and the run
; it came from (restore-of, under checkpoints).
;
; A fork copies the values its expression names into the new process,
; so each aircraft is given only what it needs, made here: naming the day
; in the fork would copy all of it, three hundred times a run.
(defun simulate (day changes targets restore every)
    (let desk $$)
    (let pids (map (lambda (i)
                       (let ctx (aircraft-context day changes i desk))
                       (let now (aircraft-at day changes i restore))
                       (let status (car now))
                       (let legs (cadr now))
                       (fork (aircraft ctx status legs)))
                   (range 0 (tuple/len (day/aircraft day)))))
    (let swaps (map (lambda (s) (match s ((a b m) (list (aircraft-named day a) (aircraft-named day b) m)))) (changes-of :swap changes)))
    (minute (tuple day pids targets every swaps) (if (nil? restore) (start) (tuple/get restore 0)) (books-at day restore)))

(defun aircraft-named (day tail) (find (lambda (i) (eq? (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i)) tail)) (range 0 (tuple/len (day/aircraft day)))))

; Aircraft i as a run starts: at its base, all its legs ahead; or as the
; checkpoint left it, its legs (a swap may have given it another's) as
; this run's changes make them.
(defun aircraft-at (day changes i restore)
    (if (nil? restore)
        (list (list :gate (cadr (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i)) 0) (legs-of day changes i))
        (match (tuple/get (tuple/get restore 1) i)
            ((status ids)
                (list (match status
                          ((:air id due) (list :air (leg-of day changes id) due))
                          (_             status))
                      (map (lambda (id) (leg-of day changes id)) ids))))))

(defun books-at (day restore)
    (if (nil? restore)
        (tuple (tuple (list 0 0 0 0) () (tuple/make (tuple/len (day/legs day)) ())) () () ())
        (match restore
            (#(_ _ waiting totals flown digests by-minute) (tuple (tuple totals waiting flown) digests by-minute ())))))

; A swap due at minute t happens before the aircraft hear it's t: the
; desk has the two aircraft's legs, and gives each the other's.
(defun minute (ctx t books)
    (match ctx
        (#(_ pids _ _ swaps)
            (let due (filter (lambda (s) (== (caddr s) t)) swaps))
            (if (nil? due)
                (tick ctx t books)
                (do (map (lambda (s) (send (nth (car s) pids) (list :legs)) (send (nth (cadr s) pids) (list :legs))) due)
                    (hear-legs ctx t books due (* 2 (length due)) ()))))))

(defun hear-legs (ctx t books due left heard)
    (if (== left 0)
        (match ctx
            (#(_ pids _ _ _)
                (map (lambda (s)
                         (match s
                             ((a b _)
                                 (send (nth a pids) (list :take (lookup b heard)))
                                 (send (nth b pids) (list :take (lookup a heard))))))
                     due)
                (tick ctx t books)))
        (recv
            ((:legs i legs) (hear-legs ctx t books due (dec left) (cons (list i legs) heard))))))

(defun tick (ctx t books)
    (match ctx
        (#(_ pids _ _ _)
            (let tick (list :tick t))
            (map (lambda (p) (send p tick)) pids)
            (hear ctx t books (length pids) ()))))

; What each aircraft said, as #(part events fuel).
(defun hear (ctx t books left said)
    (if (== left 0)
        (settle ctx t books said)
        (recv
            ((:done h events fuel) (hear ctx t books (dec left) (cons (tuple h events fuel) said))))))

(defun settle (ctx t books said)
    (match (list ctx books)
        ((#(day _ targets every _) #(ledger digests by-minute checkpoints))
            (let events (fold/l () (lambda (acc s) (append (tuple/get s 1) acc)) said))
            (let kept (keep-books day t (burnt ledger (sum (map (lambda (s) (tuple/get s 2)) said))) events))
            (let digest (hash (list (add-parts (map (lambda (s) (tuple/get s 0)) said)) (waiting-digest (tuple/get kept 1) t))))
            (let books2 (tuple kept (cons digest digests) (cons (tuple/get kept 0) by-minute) checkpoints))
            (let matched (find (lambda (g) (match g ((_ theirs from) (and (>= t from) (== (tuple/get theirs (- t (start))) digest)))))
                               targets))
            (cond
                ((cons? matched)             (finish ctx t books2 (car matched)))
                ((== (inc t) (end))          (finish ctx t books2 ()))
                ((checkpoint? every (inc t)) (checkpoint ctx t books2))
                (#true                       (minute ctx (inc t) books2))))))

(defun checkpoint? (every m) (and (> every 0) (== (% (- m (start)) every) 0)))

; Before minute t + 1, every aircraft's state, asked for, and the
; passengers waiting: (minute states waiting), the states a tuple by
; aircraft.
(defun checkpoint (ctx t books)
    (match ctx
        (#(_ pids _ _ _)
            (let ask (list :state))
            (map (lambda (p) (send p ask)) pids)
            (hear-states ctx t books (length pids) ()))))

(defun hear-states (ctx t books left states)
    (if (== left 0)
        (match books
            (#(ledger digests by-minute checkpoints)
                (let kept (list (inc t) (list->tuple (map cadr (sort-by car states))) (tuple/get ledger 1)))
                (minute ctx (inc t) (tuple ledger digests by-minute (cons kept checkpoints)))))
        (recv
            ((:state i st) (hear-states ctx t books (dec left) (cons (list i st) states))))))

(defun finish (ctx t books rejoined)
    (match (list ctx books)
        ((#(_ pids _ _ _) #(#(_ _ flown) digests by-minute checkpoints))
            (map kill pids)
            (list t rejoined (list->tuple (reverse digests)) (list->tuple (reverse by-minute)) flown (reverse checkpoints)))))

(defun burnt (ledger kg)
    (match ledger
        (#((fuel late missed cancelled) waiting flown)
            (tuple (list (+ fuel kg) late missed cancelled) waiting flown))))

; The ledger after minute t's events: arrivals, then departures, then
; cancellations, so that passengers who land as their next flight leaves
; miss it.
(defun keep-books (day t ledger events)
    (let of (lambda (kind) (map cdr (filter (lambda (e) (eq? (car e) kind)) events))))
    (fold/l (fold/l (fold/l ledger (lambda (b e) (on-arrival day t b (car e))) (of :arr))
                    (lambda (b e) (on-departure day t b (car e) (cadr e))) (of :dep))
            (lambda (b e) (on-cancel day t b (car e))) (of :cancel)))

(defun on-arrival (day t ledger id)
    (match (list (tuple/get (day/legs day) id) ledger)
        ((#(_ _ _ _ dep block pax _) #((fuel late missed cancelled) waiting flown))
            (let connecting (filter (lambda (c) (nil? (tuple/get flown (connect/out (tuple/get (day/connects day) c)))))
                                    (tuple/get (day/outs day) id)))
            (tuple (list fuel (+ late (* (max 0 (- t (+ dep block))) pax)) missed cancelled)
                   (append (map (lambda (c) (list c (+ t (change-minutes)))) connecting) waiting)
                   (tuple/set flown id (match (tuple/get flown id) ((off _ i) (list off t i))))))))

(defun on-departure (day t ledger id i)
    (match ledger
        (#((fuel late missed cancelled) waiting flown)
            (let broken (sum (map (lambda (c)
                                      (let ready (lookup c waiting))
                                      (if (and (int? ready) (<= ready t)) 0 (connect/n (tuple/get (day/connects day) c))))
                                  (tuple/get (day/ins day) id))))
            (tuple (list fuel late (+ missed broken) cancelled)
                   (remove (lambda (w) (== (connect/out (tuple/get (day/connects day) (car w))) id)) waiting)
                   (tuple/set flown id (list t () i))))))

(defun on-cancel (day t ledger id)
    (match ledger
        (#((fuel late missed cancelled) waiting flown)
            (tuple (list fuel late missed (+ cancelled (leg/pax (tuple/get (day/legs day) id))))
                   (remove (lambda (w) (== (connect/out (tuple/get (day/connects day) (car w))) id)) waiting)
                   (tuple/set flown id (list :cancelled t))))))

; The waiting part of the digest: each connection with passengers
; waiting, and how long till they can board.
(defun waiting-digest (waiting t)
    (add-parts (map (lambda (w) (part (list (car w) (max 0 (- (cadr w) t))))) waiting)))

; Parts of a digest, and their sum, modulo 2^61 - 1, a prime.
(defun prime () 2305843009213693951)
(defun part (v) (% (hash v) (prime)))
(defun add-parts (parts) (fold/l 0 (lambda (acc p) (% (+ acc p) (prime))) parts))

; --- branches -----------------------------------------------------------------

; The minutes in which a change makes what comes in differ: (from to).
(defun window (day change)
    (match change
        ((:delay flight m)
            (let dep (leg/dep (leg-named day flight)))
            (list dep (+ dep m)))
        ((:close _ from to)        (list from to))
        ((:out-of-service _ from)  (list from (end)))
        ((:quick-turn _ from to _) (list from to))
        ((:cancel flight)
            (let dep (leg/dep (leg-named day flight)))
            (list dep (inc dep)))
        ((:swap _ _ m)             (list m (inc m)))))

; A run that's been kept is #(changes parent change digests totals flown
; fate checkpoints begun): all its changes, its parent and its own change
; (() for the base); its digests, totals and legs for the whole day; (from
; until rejoined), where it was its own and the run it rejoined, or ()
; for the base; the checkpoints it kept; and the minute it began at.
(defun run/changes (r) (tuple/get r 0))
(defun run/parent (r) (tuple/get r 1))
(defun run/change (r) (tuple/get r 2))
(defun run/digests (r) (tuple/get r 3))
(defun run/totals (r) (tuple/get r 4))
(defun run/flown (r) (tuple/get r 5))
(defun run/fate (r) (tuple/get r 6))
(defun run/checkpoints (r) (tuple/get r 7))
(defun run/begun (r) (tuple/get r 8))

; The runs from the base to name, oldest first.
(defun path-of (runs name)
    (let parent (run/parent (lookup name runs)))
    (if (nil? parent) (list name) (append (path-of runs parent) (list name))))

; What a branch with change, from the last run on path, is compared with:
; each run on the path, as (name digests from), from being where the
; changes after it on the path, and change, have all stopped making a
; difference.
(defun targets-of (day runs path change)
    (match path
        (() ())
        ((name & rest)
            (let ends (map (lambda (c) (cadr (window day c))) (cons change (map (lambda (r) (run/change (lookup r runs))) rest))))
            (cons (list name (run/digests (lookup name runs)) (fold/l 0 max ends))
                  (targets-of day runs rest change)))))

; A run that rejoined name at stop, for the whole day: from stop on its
; digests are name's, its totals name's moved by what it had changed,
; and its legs name's, but for those it had flown or begun by then. One
; in the air at stop lands when name's does, the two being the same then.
(defun rejoined-day (runs name stop digests totals flown)
    (let theirs (lookup name runs))
    (let i (- stop (start)))
    (let n (- (end) (start)))
    (let shift (totals- (tuple/get totals i) (tuple/get (run/totals theirs) i)))
    (list (list->tuple (append (tuple->list digests) (tuple->list (tuple/slice (run/digests theirs) (inc i) n))))
          (list->tuple (append (tuple->list totals)
                               (map (lambda (m) (totals+ m shift)) (tuple->list (tuple/slice (run/totals theirs) (inc i) n)))))
          (rejoined-legs (run/flown theirs) flown)))

(defun rejoined-legs (theirs mine)
    (list->tuple (map (lambda (l)
                          (match (tuple/get mine l)
                              (()       (tuple/get theirs l))
                              ((off () i) (list off (cadr (tuple/get theirs l)) i))
                              (f        f)))
                      (range 0 (tuple/len mine)))))

(defun totals+ (a b) (match (list a b) (((f l m c) (f2 l2 m2 c2)) (list (+ f f2) (+ l l2) (+ m m2) (+ c c2)))))
(defun totals- (a b) (match (list a b) (((f l m c) (f2 l2 m2 c2)) (list (- f f2) (- l l2) (- m m2) (- c c2)))))

(defun against-base (runs name)
    (totals- (last-of (run/totals (lookup name runs))) (last-of (run/totals (lookup "base" runs)))))

; Whether digests a and b are the same for their first n minutes.
(defun same-before? (a b i n)
    (cond
        ((>= i n)                              #true)
        ((== (tuple/get a i) (tuple/get b i)) (same-before? a b (inc i) n))
        (#true                                 #false)))

(defun last-of (totals) (tuple/get totals (- (- (end) (start)) 1)))

; --- checkpoints ----------------------------------------------------------------

; A checkpoint is (minute states waiting), the day before that minute.
; What it doesn't hold, the totals and the legs flown so far, its run's
; whole day does, and so does the whole day of a run it holds for.

; The latest checkpoint at or before minute c that holds for run name, or
; (): one of its own, kept while it ran; one its parent held for before
; it began, when it was its parent; or, once it had rejoined a run, one
; that run held for after, the two being the same then.
(defun state-at (runs name c)
    (let r (lookup name runs))
    (let own (fold/l () (lambda (best cp) (if (<= (car cp) c) cp best)) (run/checkpoints r)))
    (let before (if (nil? (run/parent r)) () (state-at runs (run/parent r) (min c (run/begun r)))))
    (let after (match (run/fate r)
                   ((_ stop rejoined) (if (and (str? rejoined) (> c stop)) (later-than stop (state-at runs rejoined c)) ()))
                   (_                 ())))
    (fold/l () later-of (list own before after)))

(defun later-than (m cp) (if (and (cons? cp) (> (car cp) m)) cp ()))

(defun later-of (a b)
    (cond
        ((nil? a)              b)
        ((nil? b)              a)
        ((> (car b) (car a))   b)
        (#true                 a)))

; A run of a branch of name's, from checkpoint cp: #(minute states waiting
; totals flown digests by-minute), the last four name's before minute.
(defun restore-of (runs name cp)
    (match cp
        ((m states waiting)
            (let r (lookup name runs))
            (let i (- m (start)))
            (tuple m states waiting (tuple/get (run/totals r) (dec i)) (flown-at (run/flown r) m)
                   (reverse (tuple->list (tuple/slice (run/digests r) 0 i)))
                   (reverse (tuple->list (tuple/slice (run/totals r) 0 i)))))))

; The legs as they stood before minute m.
(defun flown-at (flown m)
    (list->tuple (map (lambda (f)
                          (match f
                              ((:cancelled at) (if (< at m) f ()))
                              ((off on i)      (cond
                                                   ((>= off m)                ())
                                                   ((and (int? on) (< on m))  f)
                                                   (#true                     (list off () i))))
                              (_               ())))
                      (tuple->list flown))))

; --- exploring ------------------------------------------------------------------

; Runs each branch in turn, says what it came to, and keeps it for those
; after it, passing over those kept already; then prints the history,
; writes what was asked for, and gives how many minutes it took. h is the
; day's hash, and tally is (base simulated own us saved): the minutes the
; base simulated, those the branches did, and those of their own, the
; microseconds the branches took, and those spent on the minutes before
; their changes.
(defun explore (day opts h bs runs tally)
    (match (list bs tally)
        ((() (base simulated own us saved))
            (let kept (reverse runs))
            (tty/write "the history:\n")
            (map (lambda (r) (pprint (entry-of runs r))) (filter (lambda (r) (ne? (car r) "base")) kept))
            (when (str? (opt/json opts)) (write-json (opt/json opts) day kept))
            (when (str? (opt/keep opts)) (write-history (opt/keep opts) h kept))
            (when (opt/timed opts)
                (tty/write "time: the branches in " (ms us) ", " (ms saved) " of it on the minutes before their changes" \n))
            (concat base " minutes for the base, and " simulated " for its branches, of which " own " their own"))
        ((((name parent change) & rest) _)
            (match (lookup name runs)
                (:not-found
                    (match (run-branch day opts runs name parent change tally)
                        ((runs2 tally2 said)
                            (report-branch day opts runs2 name parent change said)
                            (explore day opts h rest runs2 tally2))))
                (r
                    (tty/write name ", from " parent ": " (concat change)
                               (if (and (eq? (run/parent r) parent) (eq? (run/change r) change))
                                   ", kept"
                                   (concat ", left out: the history's " name " is another branch"))
                               \n)
                    (explore day opts h rest runs tally))))))

; One branch, run from the last checkpoint before its change: the runs
; with it, the tally, and what report-branch says of it, (same from stop
; rejoined begun took minutes).
(defun run-branch (day opts runs name parent change tally)
    (let changes (append (run/changes (lookup parent runs)) (list change)))
    (let targets (targets-of day runs (path-of runs parent) change))
    (let from (car (window day change)))
    (let every (opt/every opts))
    (let cp (if (> every 0) (state-at runs parent from) ()))
    (let restore (if (nil? cp) () (restore-of runs parent cp)))
    (let begun (if (nil? cp) (start) (car cp)))
    (let t0 (clock/us))
    (match (join (fork (simulate day changes targets restore every)))
        ((:ok (stop rejoined digests totals flown checkpoints))
            (let took (- (clock/us) t0))
            (let minutes (+ (- stop begun) 1))
            (let same (same-before? digests (run/digests (lookup parent runs)) 0 (- from (start))))
            (let whole (if (nil? rejoined) (list digests totals flown) (rejoined-day runs rejoined stop digests totals flown)))
            (let fate (list from (if (nil? rejoined) (end) stop) rejoined))
            (let runs2 (cons (list name (tuple changes parent change (car whole) (cadr whole) (caddr whole) fate checkpoints begun))
                             runs))
            (match tally
                ((base simulated own us saved)
                    (list runs2
                          (list base (+ simulated minutes) (+ own (+ (- stop from) 1)) (+ us took)
                                (+ saved (div (* took (- from begun)) minutes)))
                          (list same from stop rejoined begun took minutes)))))))

(defun report-branch (day opts runs name parent change said)
    (match said
        ((same from stop rejoined begun took minutes)
            (let d (against-base runs name))
            (tty/write name ", from " parent ": " (concat change) \n)
            (when (not same) (tty/write "    not the same as " parent " before " (clock from) \n))
            (tty/write "    the same as " parent " till " (clock from)
                       (if (nil? rejoined)
                           ", its own to the end of the day"
                           (concat ", its own till " (clock stop) ", then " rejoined "'s again"))
                       \n)
            (tty/write "    against base: fuel " (signed (nth 0 d)) " kg, " (signed (nth 1 d)) " passenger-minutes late, "
                       (signed (nth 2 d)) " missed, " (signed (nth 3 d)) " cancelled" \n)
            (when (opt/timed opts)
                (tty/write "    time: " (ms took) " for " minutes " minutes, from " (clock begun) ", " (pace day took minutes) \n)))))

; What the history says of a branch.
(defun entry-of (runs r)
    (match r
        ((name run)
            (let d (against-base runs name))
            (match (run/fate run)
                ((from until rejoined)
                    (list :branch name (list :from (run/parent run)) (list :change (run/change run))
                          (list :own (clock from) (clock until))
                          (if (nil? rejoined) (list :to-the-end) (list :rejoined rejoined))
                          (list :against-base (list :fuel (nth 0 d)) (list :late (nth 1 d))
                                              (list :missed (nth 2 d)) (list :cancelled (nth 3 d)))))))))

(defun clock (m) (concat (format-num (div m 60) 2 "0") ":" (format-num (% m 60) 2 "0")))

(defun signed (n) (if (>= n 0) (concat "+" n) (concat n)))

; Microseconds as milliseconds, to a tenth.
(defun ms (us) (concat (div us 1000) "." (div (% us 1000) 100) " ms"))

; How fast minutes went: the time for each, and the messages a second, in
; millions to a tenth, a tick and an answer for each aircraft each minute.
(defun pace (day us minutes)
    (let tenths (div (* (* 2 (tuple/len (day/aircraft day))) minutes) (max 1 (div us 10))))
    (concat (div us minutes) " µs a minute, " (div tenths 10) "." (% tenths 10) " million messages a second"))

; --- the program --------------------------------------------------------------

; The options, #(path record timed json keep from every recover).
(defun opt/path (o) (tuple/get o 0))
(defun opt/record (o) (tuple/get o 1))
(defun opt/timed (o) (tuple/get o 2))
(defun opt/json (o) (tuple/get o 3))
(defun opt/keep (o) (tuple/get o 4))
(defun opt/from (o) (tuple/get o 5))
(defun opt/every (o) (tuple/get o 6))
(defun opt/recover (o) (tuple/get o 7))

(defun read-sexps (path) (match (join (connect :fs/read path (reading ()))) ((:ok records) records)))

; What decides a run but its changes: the model, its constants, and the
; day's aircraft, legs, connections, wind and closures; not its branches
; or its record, so branches can be added to a day and its history kept.
(defun day-hash (records)
    (hash (list (model-version) (start) (end) (turn-minutes) (change-minutes) (fuel-off) (fuel-minute)
                (filter (lambda (r) (member? (car r) (list :aircraft :leg :connect :wind :closed))) records))))

; The base, simulated or kept, and then either its record, (:flew flight
; off on) for each leg that landed, or what it came to and the branches.
(defun main (opts)
    (let t0 (clock/us))
    (let records (read-sexps (opt/path opts)))
    (let day (day-of records))
    (let h (day-hash records))
    (let kept (if (str? (opt/from opts)) (history-of (opt/from opts) h) ()))
    (let t1 (clock/us))
    (when (opt/timed opts)
        (tty/write "time: the day " (if (str? (opt/from opts)) "and its history " "") "read in " (ms (- t1 t0)) ": "
                   (tuple/len (day/aircraft day)) " aircraft, "
                   (tuple/len (day/legs day)) " legs, " (tuple/len (day/connects day)) " connections" \n))
    (cond
        ((eq? kept :another-day)
            (raise (concat (opt/from opts) " was kept for another day, or another model, so it's no use for this one")))
        ((cons? kept)
            (tty/write "kept: " (length kept) " runs of this day, from " (opt/from opts) \n)
            (go-on day opts h kept 0 0))
        (#true
            (let every (opt/every opts))
            (match (join (fork (simulate day () () () every)))
                ((:ok (_ _ digests totals flown checkpoints))
                    (let t2 (clock/us))
                    (if (opt/record opts)
                        (print-record day flown)
                        (go-on day opts h (list (list "base" (tuple () () () digests totals flown () checkpoints (start))))
                               (- (end) (start)) (- t2 t1))))))))

(defun go-on (day opts h runs minutes us)
    (let base (lookup "base" runs))
    (cond
        ((str? (opt/recover opts)) (recover day opts runs))
        (#true
            (report-base day (run/flown base) (run/totals base))
            (when (and (opt/timed opts) (> minutes 0)) (tty/write "    time: " (ms us) ", " (pace day us minutes) \n))
            (explore day opts h (day/branches day) runs (list minutes 0 0 0 0)))))

(defun report-base (day flown totals)
    (let agree (length (filter (lambda (r)
                                   (match r
                                       ((flight off on)
                                           (match (tuple/get flown (index-of-leg day flight))
                                               ((off2 on2 _) (and (eq? off2 off) (eq? on2 on)))
                                               (_            #false)))))
                               (day/flew day))))
    (tty/write "the record: " (tuple/len (day/legs day)) " legs, " agree " of which the base flies as it says" \n)
    (match (last-of totals)
        ((fuel late missed cancelled)
            (tty/write "base: " (clock (start)) " to " (clock (end)) \n
                       "    fuel " fuel " kg, " late " passenger-minutes late, " missed " connections missed, "
                       cancelled " seats cancelled" \n))))

(defun index-of-leg (day flight) (index-of-loop (day/legs day) flight 0))
(defun index-of-loop (legs flight i)
    (if (eq? (leg/flight (tuple/get legs i)) flight) i (index-of-loop legs flight (inc i))))

; Its value is a record too, one nothing reads, so that the whole output
; can be appended to the day.
(defun print-record (day flown)
    (let landed (filter (lambda (l) (match (tuple/get flown l) ((:cancelled _) #false) ((off on _) (int? on)) (_ #false)))
                        (range 0 (tuple/len (day/legs day)))))
    (tty/write "; The record: when each flight left and landed, from airline --record.\n")
    (map (lambda (l)
             (match (tuple/get flown l)
                 ((off on _) (tty/write "(:flew \"" (leg/flight (tuple/get (day/legs day) l)) "\" " off " " on ")" \n))))
         landed)
    (list :recorded (length landed)))

; --- the runs, as JSON --------------------------------------------------------

; With --json, the day and every run, for charts, on one line: the legs,
; each [flight tail from to departure block passengers wind]; the
; airports' places, x and y in miles, if the day gives them; and each
; run: its parent and change, where it was its own, [from until], and the
; run it rejoined; its totals at each minute, [fuel late missed
; cancelled]; and each leg's [off on tail], null for one that didn't
; leave or land, and "cancelled".
(defun write-json (path day runs)
    (spew path (list (json/print (day-json day runs)))))

(defun day-json (day runs)
    (list :object
          (list "start" (start))
          (list "end" (end))
          (list "airports" (map (lambda (a)
                                    (match a
                                        ((code x y hub) (list :object (list "code" code) (list "x" x) (list "y" y) (list "hub" hub)))))
                                (day/airports day)))
          (list "legs" (map (lambda (l)
                                (match l
                                    (#(flight a from to dep block pax wind)
                                        (list flight (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) a)) from to dep block pax wind))))
                            (tuple->list (day/legs day))))
          (list "runs" (map (lambda (r) (run-json day r)) runs))))

(defun or-null (v) (if (nil? v) :null v))

(defun run-json (day r)
    (match r
        ((name #(_ parent change _ totals flown fate _ _))
            (list :object
                  (list "name" name)
                  (list "parent" (or-null parent))
                  (list "change" (if (nil? change) :null (cons (symbol->string (car change)) (cdr change))))
                  (list "own" (match fate ((from until _) (list from until)) (_ :null)))
                  (list "rejoined" (match fate ((_ _ rejoined) (or-null rejoined)) (_ :null)))
                  (list "totals" totals)
                  (list "flown" (map (lambda (f)
                                         (match f
                                             (()             :null)
                                             ((:cancelled _) "cancelled")
                                             ((off on i)     (list off (or-null on) (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i))))))
                                     (tuple->list flown)))))))

; --- recovering from a disruption ---------------------------------------------

; With --recover file, a disruption and remedies for it: the disruption a
; branch of the base, each remedy a branch of the disruption. Then, in
; rounds, the candidates (doing nothing among them) that no other left is
; better than in all of passenger-minutes late, connections missed and
; seats cancelled are sent to the services that check them, till as many
; as the budget have been; and those that pass to the one that ranks
; them. The file has:
;
;     (:disruption name change)  what happened, as a branch's change
;     (:try change)              a remedy to try, as many as wanted
;     (:services crew maintenance rank)
;                                the services' URLs; without it, the
;                                stand-ins in airline-services.slight
;     (:check n)                 the budget, 12 if it doesn't say
;     (:top n)                   how many of those ranked to show, 3
;
; Remedies are also made: holds, each flight leaving after the disruption
; that passengers connect to, held 15, 30 and 45 minutes; cancellations,
; each flight leaving after it; and swaps, each two aircraft at the first
; minute after it they're both on the ground at one airport, if either
; has a leg ahead then. What a service is sent, every leg's flight, tail,
; times and fate, has nothing of anyone in it (airline-services.slight
; says how it's sent and answered).
(defun recover (day opts runs)
    (let asked (read-sexps (opt/recover opts)))
    (match (find (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) :disruption)) asked)
        ((_ dname dchange)
            (match (run-branch day opts runs dname "base" dchange (list 0 0 0 0 0))
                ((runs2 _ _)
                    (let now (car (window day dchange)))
                    (let d (against-base runs2 dname))
                    (tty/write "the disruption, " dname ": " (concat dchange) ", from " (clock now) \n
                               "    against base: fuel " (signed (nth 0 d)) " kg, " (signed (nth 1 d)) " passenger-minutes late, "
                               (signed (nth 2 d)) " missed, " (signed (nth 3 d)) " cancelled" \n)
                    (let cands (candidates day (lookup dname runs2) now (map cadr (filter (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) :try)) asked))))
                    (let runs3 (try-all day opts runs2 dname cands 1))
                    (let names (cons "c0" (map (lambda (i) (concat "c" i)) (range 1 (inc (length cands))))))
                    (let run-of (lambda (n) (if (eq? n "c0") dname n)))
                    (let rejoined (length (filter (lambda (n) (str? (caddr (run/fate (lookup n runs3))))) (cdr names))))
                    (tty/write "the candidates: " (length cands) " remedies, and nothing; " rejoined
                               " of the remedies rejoin a run before them" \n)
                    (let services (services-of day asked))
                    (let ctx (tuple day
                                    (map (lambda (n) (list n (operated day (lookup (run-of n) runs3)))) names)
                                    (zip names (cons "nothing" (map (lambda (c) (concat c)) cands)))
                                    (map (lambda (n) (list n (cdr (against-base runs3 (run-of n))))) names)
                                    (car services) (setting asked :check 12)))
                    (let told (match (shortlist ctx names () 0 1)
                                  ((:ok passed checked) (tell-ranked ctx passed checked (length cands) (setting asked :top 3)))
                                  ((:error why)         (concat "stopped: " why))))
                    (map kill (cadr services))
                    told)))
        (_ (concat (opt/recover opts) " says no (:disruption name change)"))))

(defun setting (asked key default)
    (match (find (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) key)) asked)
        ((_ v) v)
        (_     default)))

; Each remedy run, a branch of the disruption, as c1, c2 and on.
(defun try-all (day opts runs from cands i)
    (match cands
        (() runs)
        ((c & rest)
            (match (run-branch day opts runs (concat "c" i) from c (list 0 0 0 0 0))
                ((runs2 _ _) (try-all day opts runs2 from rest (inc i)))))))

; The remedies to try, in order, none twice: those asked for, then holds,
; cancellations and swaps (above, recover).
(defun candidates (day run now tries)
    (let flown (run/flown run))
    (let alive (filter (lambda (l) (and (>= (leg/dep (tuple/get (day/legs day) l)) now) (not (cancelled? (tuple/get flown l)))))
                       (range 0 (tuple/len (day/legs day)))))
    (let holds (fold/r () (lambda (l acc)
                              (if (cons? (tuple/get (day/ins day) l))
                                  (append (map (lambda (m) (list :delay (leg/flight (tuple/get (day/legs day) l)) m)) (list 15 30 45)) acc)
                                  acc))
                       alive))
    (let cancels (map (lambda (l) (list :cancel (leg/flight (tuple/get (day/legs day) l)))) alive))
    (reverse (fold/l () (lambda (acc c) (if (member? c acc) acc (cons c acc)))
                     (append tries (append holds (append cancels (swaps-for day flown now)))))))

(defun cancelled? (f) (match f ((:cancelled _) #true) (_ #false)))

; Each two aircraft, x before y, at the first minute from now they're both
; on the ground at one airport, if either has a leg ahead then.
(defun swaps-for (day flown now)
    (let n (tuple/len (day/aircraft day)))
    (let spans (list->tuple (map (lambda (i) (spans-of day flown i)) (range 0 n))))
    (fold/r () (lambda (x acc) (append (filter cons? (map (lambda (y) (swap-of day flown spans now x y)) (range (inc x) n))) acc))
            (range 0 n)))

(defun swap-of (day flown spans now x y)
    (let starts (fold/r () (lambda (a acc)
                               (fold/r acc (lambda (b acc2)
                                               (match (list a b)
                                                   (((s1 e1 p1) (s2 e2 p2))
                                                       (let m (max now (max s1 s2)))
                                                       (if (and (eq? p1 p2) (<= m (min e1 e2))) (cons m acc2) acc2))))
                                       (tuple/get spans y)))
                        (tuple/get spans x)))
    (if (nil? starts)
        ()
        (do (let m (fold/l (car starts) min (cdr starts)))
            (let ahead (filter (lambda (l) (match (tuple/get flown l) ((off _ i) (and (or (== i x) (== i y)) (>= off m))) (_ #false)))
                               (range 0 (tuple/len flown))))
            (if (nil? ahead) () (list :swap (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) x)) (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) y)) m)))))

; An aircraft's spans on the ground, (from to airport), from the start of
; a minute to the start of another: before its first departure, at its
; base; between a landing and its next departure; after its last landing,
; to the end of the day.
(defun spans-of (day flown i)
    (let mine (sort-by car (filter cons? (map (lambda (l) (match (tuple/get flown l) ((off on j) (if (== j i) (list off on l) ())) (_ ())))
                                              (range 0 (tuple/len flown))))))
    (spans-loop day mine (start) (cadr (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i)) ()))

(defun spans-loop (day legs since at acc)
    (match legs
        (() (reverse (cons (list since (dec (end)) at) acc)))
        (((off on l) & rest)
            (if (int? on)
                (spans-loop day rest (inc on) (tuple/get (tuple/get (day/legs day) l) 3) (cons (list since off at) acc))
                (reverse (cons (list since off at) acc))))))

; The day a run flew, as the services are sent it: every leg's flight, the
; aircraft that flew it, when it left and landed, and what became of it.
(defun operated (day run)
    (map (lambda (l)
             (let flight (leg/flight (tuple/get (day/legs day) l)))
             (match (tuple/get (run/flown run) l)
                 ((:cancelled _) (list flight :null :null :null "cancelled"))
                 ((off on i)     (list flight (car (tuple/get (day/aircraft day) i)) off (or-null on) (if (int? on) "landed" "in the air")))
                 (_              (list flight :null :null :null "not flown"))))
         (range 0 (tuple/len (day/legs day)))))

; The services' URLs, (crew maintenance rank), and the pids of any
; stand-ins started for them, to stop after.
(defun services-of (day asked)
    (match (find (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) :services)) asked)
        ((_ crew maintenance rank) (list (list crew maintenance rank) ()))
        (_
            (let started (map stand-in (list (crew-service day) (maintenance-service day) (rank-service day))))
            (list (map car started) (map cadr started)))))

; A stand-in, listening where the system says: its URL and its pid.
(defun stand-in (handler)
    (match (join (fork (serve-for handler)))
        ((:ok (port pid)) (list (concat "http://127.0.0.1:" port "/") pid))))

(defun serve-for (handler)
    (let server (http/serve 0 handler))
    (recv ((:listening port) (list port server))))

; A service's results for candidates, each (name flights): (:ok results),
; each (name members), or (:error why).
(defun ask-service (url candidates)
    (let body (json/print (list :object (list "candidates" (map (lambda (c) (list :object (list "name" (car c)) (list "flights" (cadr c))))
                                                                candidates)))))
    (match (http/request :post url (list (list "content-type" "application/json")) body)
        ((:ok (200 _ text))
            (match (json/parse text)
                ((:ok (:object & members))
                    (list :ok (map (lambda (r) (match r ((:object & fields) (list (lookup "name" fields) fields)))) (lookup "results" members))))
                (_ (list :error (concat url " answered with what isn't JSON")))))
        ((:ok (status _ _)) (list :error (concat url " answered " status)))
        ((:error reason)    (list :error (concat url ": " reason)))))

; ctx is #(day operated labels measures urls budget): each candidate's
; operated day, its label and (late missed cancelled) against the base,
; by name; the services' URLs; and the budget. Gives (:ok passed checked)
; or (:error why).
(defun shortlist (ctx rest passed checked k)
    (cond
        ((or (nil? rest) (>= checked (tuple/get ctx 5))) (list :ok passed checked))
        (#true
            (let ms (tuple/get ctx 3))
            (let front (filter (lambda (n) (not (bettered? ms n rest))) rest))
            (tty/write "round " k ": the " (length front) " candidates no other left betters in late, missed and cancelled together" \n)
            (match (verdicts ctx front)
                ((:ok said)
                    (map (lambda (n) (tell-verdict ctx n (lookup n said))) front)
                    (shortlist ctx (remove (lambda (n) (member? n front)) rest)
                               (append passed (filter (lambda (n) (nil? (lookup n said))) front))
                               (+ checked (length front)) (inc k)))
                (failed failed)))))

; Whether another of rest is as good as n in all three, and better in one.
(defun bettered? (ms n rest)
    (let mine (lookup n ms))
    (not (nil? (find (lambda (o) (let theirs (lookup o ms)) (and (ne? theirs mine) (all-at-most? theirs mine))) rest))))

(defun all-at-most? (a b)
    (match (list a b) (((x1 y1 z1) (x2 y2 z2)) (and (<= x1 x2) (and (<= y1 y2) (<= z1 z2))))))

; Each candidate's reasons, from the crew service and then the
; maintenance one, each (service what why): (:ok ((name reasons) ...)).
(defun verdicts (ctx front)
    (let sent (map (lambda (n) (list n (lookup n (tuple/get ctx 1)))) front))
    (let urls (tuple/get ctx 4))
    (match (list (ask-service (car urls) sent) (ask-service (cadr urls) sent))
        (((:ok crew) (:ok maintenance))
            (list :ok (map (lambda (n) (list n (append (reasons-of "crew" (lookup n crew)) (reasons-of "maintenance" (lookup n maintenance)))))
                           front)))
        (((:error why) _) (list :error why))
        ((_ (:error why)) (list :error why))))

(defun reasons-of (service fields)
    (map (lambda (r) (match r ((:object & f) (list service (lookup "what" f) (lookup "why" f))))) (lookup "reasons" fields)))

(defun tell-verdict (ctx n reasons)
    (match (lookup n (tuple/get ctx 3))
        ((late missed cancelled)
            (tty/write "    " n " " (lookup n (tuple/get ctx 2)) ": late " (signed late) ", missed " (signed missed)
                       ", cancelled " (signed cancelled) \n)
            (if (nil? reasons)
                (tty/write "        passes" \n)
                (map (lambda (r) (match r ((service what why) (tty/write "        " service ": " what ": " why \n)))) reasons)))))

; Those that passed, ranked by the ranking service's cost, ties in the
; order they passed; the first top of them told.
(defun tell-ranked (ctx passed checked tried top)
    (tty/write "ranked by the ranking service, of those that pass:" \n)
    (match (if (nil? passed) (list :ok ()) (ask-service (caddr (tuple/get ctx 4)) (map (lambda (n) (list n (lookup n (tuple/get ctx 1)))) passed)))
        ((:ok scores)
            (let ranked (sort-by (lambda (n) (lookup "cost" (lookup n scores))) passed))
            (map (lambda (p)
                     (match p
                         ((place n)
                             (let s (lookup n scores))
                             (tty/write "    " place ". " n " " (lookup n (tuple/get ctx 2)) ": cost " (lookup "cost" s) ": "
                                        (lookup "disrupted" s) " passengers disrupted, " (lookup "refunds" s) " refunded, "
                                        (lookup "compensated" s) " compensated, " (lookup "misconnected" s) " misconnected, "
                                        (lookup "late" s) " passenger-minutes late" \n))))
                 (zip (range 1 (inc top)) ranked))
            (concat tried " remedies, " checked " checked, " (length passed) " that pass, and the best "
                    (if (nil? ranked) "none" (car ranked))))
        ((:error why) (concat "stopped: " why))))

; --- the history, kept ---------------------------------------------------------

; With --keep, every run, for a later --from: (:kept-for h), the day's
; hash, then (:run name changes parent change digests totals flown fate
; checkpoints begun) for each run, oldest first, a line each.
(defun write-history (path h runs)
    (spew path (cons (sexp/print (list :kept-for h))
                     (map (lambda (r) (match r ((name run) (sexp/print (cons :run (cons name (tuple->list run))))))) runs))))

; The runs a history kept, newest first as they're kept here, or
; :another-day if it was kept for another.
(defun history-of (path h)
    (let records (read-sexps path))
    (if (member? (list :kept-for h) records)
        (reverse (map (lambda (r) (match r ((:run name & fields) (list name (list->tuple fields)))))
                      (filter (lambda (r) (eq? (car r) :run)) records)))
        :another-day))

(defun options (args o)
    (match args
        (()                    (main o))
        (("--record" & rest)   (options rest (tuple/set o 1 #true)))
        (("--time" & rest)     (options rest (tuple/set o 2 #true)))
        (("--json" f & rest)   (options rest (tuple/set o 3 f)))
        (("--keep" f & rest)   (options rest (tuple/set o 4 f)))
        (("--from" f & rest)   (options rest (tuple/set o 5 f)))
        (("--every" n & rest)  (options rest (tuple/set o 6 (or-0 (string->int n)))))
        (("--recover" f & rest) (options rest (tuple/set o 7 f)))
        ((p & rest)            (options rest (tuple/set o 0 p)))))

(options @ARGV (tuple "examples/airline-day.sexp" #false #false #false #false #false 30 #false))
